== Specifications and performance ==
The main carry over component from the [[Bugatti Veyron|Veyron]] is the {{cvt|7993|cc|L cuin|1|abbr=on}} quad-[[turbocharged]] [[W16 engine]], though it is heavily updated. The engine in the Chiron has a peak power output of {{convert|1103|kW|hp PS|0|abbr=on}} at 6,700 rpm and {{convert|1600|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}} of torque starting from 2,000 to 6,000 rpm.<ref>{{Cite web|title=180301_Bugatti_Chiron_en.pdf|url=https://www.bugatti.com/fileadmin/media/Media/MediaKit/180301_Bugatti_Chiron_en.pdf|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201108104909/https://www.bugatti.com/fileadmin/media/Media/MediaKit/180301_Bugatti_Chiron_en.pdf|archive-date=8 November 2020|access-date=23 August 2020}}</ref> The engine in the most powerful variant of its predecessor, the [[Bugatti Veyron#Bugatti Veyron 16.4 Super Sport, World Record Edition (2010–2011)|Veyron Super Sport]], generates {{convert|221|kW|hp PS|0|abbr=on}} less than the new Chiron, while the engine in the original Veyron generates {{cvt|367|kW|hp PS|0|abbr=on}} less power.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.bugatti.com/fileadmin/media/Media/Veyron/Veyron_16.4/Technical_Specifications_Bugatti_Veyron_16.4.pdf |title=Bugatti Veyron 16.4 – Technical Specifications |publisher=Bugatti |date=2018-05-04 |access-date=2018-05-05 |archive-date=2018-04-27 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180427120253/https://www.bugatti.com/fileadmin/media/Media/Veyron/Veyron_16.4/Technical_Specifications_Bugatti_Veyron_16.4.pdf |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.autoexpress.co.uk/bugatti/92681/bugatti-chiron-everything-we-know-so-far-about-the-1479bhp-hypercar |title=Bugatti Chiron: everything we know about the 1,479bhp hypercar |first=Jonathan |last=Burn |work=Auto Express |location=UK |date=2016-08-22 |access-date=2016-10-28 |archive-date=2016-06-24 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160624122753/http://www.autoexpress.co.uk/bugatti/92681/bugatti-chiron-everything-we-know-so-far-about-the-1479bhp-hypercar |url-status=live }}</ref>

