On 8 September 2019, Bugatti presented a limited production high performance variant of the Chiron called the Chiron Super Sport 300+ to owners taking part in the company's 110th-anniversary tour in Europe.<ref>{{cite press release |title=Bugatti Chiron Super Sport 300+ – A Gift to Celebrate the Record |url=https://newsroom.bugatti.com/press-releases/bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300-plus |access-date=23 December 2022 |publisher=Bugatti |date=9 September 2019 |location=Molsheim}}</ref> The variant is limited to 30 examples at a net unit price of 3.5 million euros. Changes from the standard Chiron include a more powerful engine, increased top speed, and a characteristic paint scheme featuring a lacquer-coated carbon fibre body with orange stripes, echoing the aesthetics of the company's previous top speed record-breaking cars, the [[Bugatti Veyron|Veyron]] Super Sport World Record Edition and the [[Bugatti Veyron|Veyron]] Grand Sport Vitesse World Record Car.

The car is powered by a {{cvt|1600|PS|PS kW hp|round=5|abbr=on|order=out}} quad-turbocharged W16 engine shared with the [[Bugatti Centodieci]], nicknamed "Thor". This car has a grey Bugatti logo made of black enamel and silver, the exhaust system from the Centodieci, a modified gearbox with longer ratios and front and rear bumpers optimised for aerodynamics at high speed, resulting in the overall length increase of the car by {{cvt|9.8|in|mm|1|abbr=on|order=flip}}.

The Super Sport 300+ was also equipped with a top speed limiter, akin to the one found in the standard Chiron. Without the limiter, Bugatti claimed the car could attain a maximum speed in excess of {{cvt|300|mph|kph|0|abbr=on|order=flip}}, with {{cvt|304.7|mph|kph|0|abbr=on|order=flip}} being achieved in August 2019 with a pre-production model. Bugatti also prepared the cars of owners who want to take the car to its full potential at the Ehra-Lessien test track.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.caranddriver.com/news/a28927762/bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300-photos-info/ |title=Bugatti Launches Limited Chiron Super Sport 300+, World's Fastest Production Car |first=Mike |last=Duff |work=Car & Driver |url-status=live |date=2019-09-08 |access-date=2019-09-08 |archive-date=2019-10-04 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191004174726/https://www.caranddriver.com/news/a28927762/bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300-photos-info/ }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/supercars/bugatti-chiron-super-sport-production-300mph-car |title=The Bugatti Chiron Super Sport+ is a production 300mph car |work=Top Gear |location=UK |date=2019-09-08 |access-date=2019-09-08 |archive-date=2020-11-08 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201108104910/https://www.topgear.com/car-news/supercars/bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300-production-300mph-car |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.carthrottle.com/post/the-42m-bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300-has-arrived/ |title=The £4.2m Bugatti Chiron Super Sport 300+ Has Arrived |first=Matt |last=Robinson |work=CarThrottle |date=2019-09-09 |access-date=2019-09-09 |archive-date=2019-09-09 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190909093257/https://www.carthrottle.com/post/the-42m-bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300-has-arrived/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.topspeed.com/cars/bugatti/2020-bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300/ |title=Bugatti's Chiron Super Sport 300+ is the fastest car on Earth. Or is it? |last=Rus |first=Tudor |work=Top Speed |location=UK |url-status=live |date=2019-09-11 |access-date=2019-09-30 |archive-date=2020-11-08 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201108104910/https://www.topspeed.com/cars/bugatti/2020-bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300-ar186525.html }}</ref><ref name="S484">{{Cite web|url=https://www.bugatti.com/media/news/2019/bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300/|title=Bugatti Chiron Super Sport 300+|website=www.bugatti.com|language=en|access-date=2019-10-16|archive-date=2019-10-16|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191016094330/https://www.bugatti.com/media/news/2019/bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300/|url-status=live}}</ref>

The first eight were delivered in September 2021.<ref>{{cite press release |title=First Bugatti Chiron Super Sport 300+ Ready for Launch |url=https://newsroom.bugatti.com/press-releases/first-bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300-ready-for-launch |access-date=23 December 2022 |publisher=Bugatti |date=23 September 2021 |location=Molsheim}}</ref>

Bugatti delivered the final Chiron Super Sport 300+ on 21 July 2022.<ref>{{cite press release |title=Final world record-breaking Bugatti Chiron Super Sport 300+ delivered |url=https://www.bugatti.com/media/news/2022/final-world-record-breaking-bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300-delivered/ |publisher=Bugatti |location=[[Molsheim, France]] |date=21 July 2022 |access-date=22 December 2022 |archive-date=2023-03-25  |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230325022827/https://www.bugatti.com/media/news/2022/final-world-record-breaking-bugatti-chiron-super-sport-300-delivered/ |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Bugatti Delivers Final Chiron Super Sport 300+, Its Fastest, And Weirdly, Greenest Car |url=https://www.carscoops.com/2022/07/bugatti-delivers-final-chiron-super-sport-300-its-fastest-and-weirdly-greenest-car/ |first=Chris |last=Chilton |work=Carscoops |location=US |date=21 July 2022 |access-date=22 December 2022}}</ref>

