=== Chiron Noire (2020)  ===
Bugatti announced a special-edition, the Chiron Noire, celebrating the 1936 [[Bugatti Type 57#Type 57S/SC|Bugatti Type 57SC]] Coupé Aero No. 57453 (also known as "La Voiture Noire") following the 2019 one-off homage and namesake "La Voiture Noire".<ref>{{cite press release |title=Bugatti Edition "Chiron Noire" – Exclusive Special Model |url=https://newsroom.bugatti.com/press-releases/bugatti-edition-chiron-noire-exclusive-special-model |access-date=23 December 2022 |publisher=Bugatti |date=29 November 2019 |location=Molsheim}}</ref> The special edition comes in two versions, the Noire Élégance (black exposed carbon body) and the Noire Sportive (black exposed carbon body covered with a matte black finish). Only 20 were made. The Noire starts at around $3.3 million, and deliveries are expected to begin in mid-2020.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.caranddriver.com/news/a30079933/bugatti-chiron-noire-special-edition/|title=Bugatti Chiron Noire: Budget Version of World's Priciest New Car|date=2019-12-02|access-date=2020-06-03|archive-date=2020-05-18|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200518010244/https://www.caranddriver.com/news/a30079933/bugatti-chiron-noire-special-edition/|url-status=live}}</ref> The Chiron Noire package is available for the entry-level Chiron or the Chiron Sport, in this case at an extra charge of {{euro|100,000}}.<ref>{{cite press release |url=https://www.bugatti.com/media/news/2019/bugatti-edition-chiron-noire/ |title=New edition model of the Chiron inspired by the most beautiful car in the world |publisher=Bugatti Automobiles S.A.S. |location=[[Molsheim, France]] |date=2 December 2019 |access-date=2021-01-26}}</ref>

