The Chiron Profilée is a one-off special introduced in December 2022. It is based on the Chiron Pur Sport, but features a new aerodynamic profile characterized by wider air dams and a bigger grille up front, a redesigned front splitter, and a relatively small rear wing with a hollow middle section. Bugatti also made changes to the steering and suspension systems, and it gave the seven-speed, dual-clutch automatic transmission 15% shorter gear ratios. It is the fastest-accelerating car of the Chiron range with a {{convert|0-100|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}} of 2.3 seconds. {{convert|0-200|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}} takes 5.5 seconds and {{convert|0-300|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}} takes 12.4 seconds. It has a top speed of {{convert|380|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}}. It's finished in silver (Argent Atlantique) and the bottom part of the car features bare carbon fiber that's tinted in blue (Bleu Royal Carbon). It is the first Chiron fitted with woven leather on the dashboard, the center console and the door panels.<ref>{{cite web |title=Bugatti Chiron Profilée One-Off W16 Hypercar Heads To Auction |url=https://www.motor1.com/news/627679/bugatti-chiron-profilee-revealed/ |website=www.motor1.com |access-date=22 December 2022}}</ref>

Bugatti had planned to build 30 units, but as the production of its pre-series vehicle started, all 500 Chiron slots were already assigned. The project was cancelled and the car never entered production thus only one example was built and it is fully street-legal in European markets. On the 1 February 2023, the Profilée was sold at auction by RM Sotheby's for {{euro|9,792,500|link=yes}}, with a percentage of the proceeds going to benefit charitable causes. At the time of its sale, it was believed to be the last street-legal W16-powered car Bugatti sold, as the Chiron and the Mistral were already sold-out.<ref name="Solitaire">{{cite press release |title=The Bugatti Chiron Profilée: An Automotive Solitaire |url=https://newsroom.bugatti.com/press-releases/the-bugatti-chiron-profilee-an-automotive-solitaire |access-date=23 December 2022 |date=21 December 2022 |location=Molsheim}}</ref>

==Other Bugatti based on the Chiron==
=== La Voiture Noire (2019) ===
{{multiple image
| align             = right
| direction         = vertical
| width             = 200
| image1            = La Voiture Noire in St. Moritz, Switzerland.jpg
| image2            = Bugatti La Voiture Noire, GIMS 2019, Le Grand-Saconnex (GIMS0948).jpg
| footer            = The Bugatti La Voiture Noire; note the six exhaust pipes at the rear of the car and the illuminated Bugatti lettering
}}

The La Voiture Noire is a one-off special introduced at the [[Geneva Motor Show#2019|2019 Geneva Motor Show]]. Based on the Chiron, the design of the car harkens back to the [[Bugatti Type 57|Type 57 SC Atlantic]] and is a celebration of the company's distinctive design history. The car has a hand-built body made from carbon fibre designed by Bugatti designer Etienne Salomé which has an elongated nose (similar to that on the [[Bugatti Divo|Divo]]) and an elongated back section. Other notable features include unique wing mirrors, LED taillight strip, and wheels. Unlike the original, the car has a mid-engine layout.

A trim piece running from the front of the car to the rear spoiler recalls the dorsal fin present on the Type 57 SC. The car features a floating windscreen and has masked A-pillars. The La Voiture Noire shares many design similarities with the Bugatti Rembrandt, a cancelled front-engine grand tourer powered by the Chiron's W16 engine.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Horncastle|first=Rowan|date=2020-02-17|title=These are Bugatti's secret concept cars|url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/concept/these-are-bugattis-secret-concept-cars|url-status=live|access-date=2021-07-04|website=Top Gear|language=en|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200218141722/https://www.topgear.com/car-news/concept/these-are-bugattis-secret-concept-cars |archive-date=2020-02-18 }}</ref>

The La Voiture Noire is powered by the same 8.0-litre quad-turbocharged W16 engine from the Chiron having the same power output figures but the 7-speed dual-clutch gearbox and the all-wheel-drive system are heavily revised in order to allow for a more relaxed driving experience. Softer dampers and a revised chassis contribute to the factor. The car features six exhaust pipes recalling the innovative design of the past.

Performance figures remain unknown but the company states that the car is likely to have lower top speed and acceleration times as compared to the Chiron due to its Grand Touring nature. The car sold for {{GBP|9.5 million}}, which makes it one of the most expensive cars built to date.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/bugatti/106184/new-one-off-bugatti-la-voiture-noire-revealed-at-geneva |title=New one-off Bugatti La Voiture Noire revealed at Geneva |work=[[Auto Express]] |date=2019-03-05 |access-date=2019-03-05 |archive-date=2019-03-05 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190305151058/https://www.autoexpress.co.uk/bugatti/106184/new-one-off-bugatti-la-voiture-noire-revealed-at-geneva |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.designboom.com/technology/bugatti-la-voiture-noire-hypercar-03-05-2019/ |title=one-off Bugatti la Voiture Noire reinterprets the type 57 SC Atlantic |date=2019-03-05 |work=Design boom |access-date=2019-03-05 |archive-date=2019-03-06 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190306043401/https://www.designboom.com/technology/bugatti-la-voiture-noire-hypercar-03-05-2019/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

A statement made later by the company confirmed that the car on display was a concept car and that the final product would take two and a half years more to complete. The show car had electric motors instead of an engine for easy maneuverability.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.zero2turbo.com/2019/03/two-years-before-the-bugatti-la-voiture-noire-is-actually-completed.html|title=Two Years Before The Bugatti La Voiture Noire Is Actually Completed|date=2019-03-20|first=Barrie|last=Ferreira|publisher=Zero2Turbo|access-date=2019-03-20|archive-date=2019-03-24|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190324162816/https://www.zero2turbo.com/2019/03/two-years-before-the-bugatti-la-voiture-noire-is-actually-completed.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name=carscoops2019-03-19>{{cite web |url=https://www.carscoops.com/2019/03/bugatti-needs-two-more-years-to-finish-off-the-la-voiture-noire/ |title=Bugatti Needs Two More Years To Finish Off The La Voiture Noire |website=Carscoops |date=2019-03-19 |access-date=2019-03-20 |author=Cristian Gnaticov |quote=it has yet to receive the 8.0-liter quad-turbo W-16 engine .. Bugatti fitted the display model with an electric powertrain |archive-date=2019-03-22 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190322061039/https://www.carscoops.com/2019/03/bugatti-needs-two-more-years-to-finish-off-the-la-voiture-noire/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Unlike the show car, the production La Voiture Noire features a Havana Brown leather interior and a fully functional drivetrain, powered by the Chiron’s W16 engine.

According to Exclusive Car Registry, La Voiture Noire is owned by a member of the Piëch family after [[Ferdinand Piëch]], the man for whom it was originally commissioned, died before receiving it.

=== Bugatti F.K.P. Hommage (2026) ===
[[File:2026 Bugatti FKP Hommage USG26.jpg|thumb|Bugatti F.K.P Hommage]]

The F.K.P. Hommage is a one-off special introduced in a press conference. Based on the Chiron, the design paid homage to the [[Bugatti Veyron]] honoring 20 years since its debut. The name is based on the initials [[Ferdinand Piëch|Ferdinand Karl Piëch]], former chairman of the executive board (Vorstandsvorsitzender) of the [[Volkswagen Group]]. This is the final car in Bugatti's lineup to have the W16 engine.<ref>{{Cite web|date=2026-01-22|title=BUGATTI F.K.P. HOMMAGE|url=https://www.bugatti.com/en/solitaire/fkp-hommage|language=en }}</ref>

