==Marketing==
The Chiron was recreated in [[Lego]] as 2018's biennial [[Lego Technic|Technic]] [[sports car]]. It was released on 1 June 2018 as a 1:8 [[Lego Technic#Set42083|scale model]] with 3,600 individual parts.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://brickset.com/article/34833/42083-bugatti-chiron-to-be-released-in-june/|title=42083 Bugatti Chiron to be released in June.|work=Brickset.com|location=UK|date=2018-03-11|access-date=2018-03-11|archive-date=2018-06-20|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180620124751/https://brickset.com/article/34833/42083-bugatti-chiron-to-be-released-in-june/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 30 August 2018, Lego unveiled a working full-sized model of the Chiron. It was constructed almost entirely with Lego Technic elements (339 unique types, over 1,000,000 pieces in total) with exceptions for the Bugatti badge, the wheels, a steel frame, a steel roll cage, a steel drive chain and the seat belts. The engine was created from 2,304 Lego Power Function motors found in standard models; it was estimated to produce {{Convert|4|kW|hp |1|abbr=on}} and {{Convert|92|Nm|lbft|0|abbr=on}} of torque. The car was test driven by [[Andy Wallace (racing driver)|Andy Wallace]], Bugatti's official test driver, at [[Volkswagen]]'s Ehra-Lessien test track.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.lego.com/en-us/themes/technic/bugatti-chiron/build-for-real?icmp=COXXXXHomeMSXTechnicProduct42083BuildForReal|title=With LEGO Technic we like to state that you build for real. And to prove this is, we decided to build a car – a life-size LEGO Technic car!|publisher=Lego|access-date=2018-08-31|archive-date=2018-09-01|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180901044519/https://www.lego.com/en-us/themes/technic/bugatti-chiron/build-for-real?icmp=COXXXXHomeMSXTechnicProduct42083BuildForReal|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/supercars/behold-full-size-lego-bugatti-chiron |title=Behold: the full-size Lego Bugatti Chiron! |first=Vijay |last=Pattni |work=Top Gear |location=UK |date=2018-08-30 |access-date=2018-10-07 |archive-date=2018-10-07 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181007040227/https://www.topgear.com/car-news/supercars/behold-full-size-lego-bugatti-chiron |url-status=live }}</ref> Top speed is {{cvt|20|km/h|mph|0}}.<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n-RtJOfFlZU |title=See how it was made - The Amazing Life-Size LEGO Technic version of the Bugatti Chiron |publisher=Lego Youtube Channel |date=2018-08-31 |access-date=2021-06-14 |via=Youtube}}</ref>

